<comment datatype="string">&lt;a href="/gene?orgid=META&amp;id=MONOMER-17874"&gt;&lt;i&gt;S&lt;/i&gt;-methyl-5'-thioadenosine phosphorylase&lt;/a&gt; was shown to catalyze the reversible phosphorylation of &lt;a href="/compound?orgid=META&amp;id=5-METHYLTHIOADENOSINE"&gt;&lt;i&gt;S&lt;/i&gt;-methyl-5'-thioadenosine&lt;/a&gt; (MTA) to &lt;a href="/compound?orgid=META&amp;id=ADENINE"&gt;adenine&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="/compound?orgid=META&amp;id=CPD-444"&gt;&lt;i&gt;S&lt;/i&gt;-methyl-5-thio-&amp;alpha;-D-ribose 1-phosphate&lt;/a&gt; in a singe step (unlike the case in some bacteria, where this conversion is catalyzed in two steps by the enzymes encoded by &lt;a href="/gene?orgid=META&amp;id=G-824"&gt;mtnN&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="/gene?orgid=META&amp;id=G-830"&gt;mtnK&lt;/a&gt; (see &lt;a href="/META/NEW-IMAGE?type=PATHWAY&amp;object=PWY-6754"&gt;&lt;i&gt;S&lt;/i&gt;-methyl-5'-thioadenosine degradation I&lt;/a&gt;) [&lt;a href="http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/23042035"&gt;Erb12&lt;/a&gt;].
&lt;p&gt;

The &lt;a href="/gene?orgid=META&amp;id=G-15516"&gt;mtnP&lt;/a&gt; gene of &lt;a href="/META/NEW-IMAGE?object=TAX-1085"&gt;&lt;i&gt;Rhodospirillum rubrum&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt; was cloned and expressed in &lt;a href="/META/NEW-IMAGE?object=TAX-562"&gt;&lt;i&gt;Escherichia coli&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, and the recombinant protein was purified and characterized &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt;. It was found that the enzyme is active with both &lt;a href="/compound?orgid=META&amp;id=5-METHYLTHIOADENOSINE"&gt;&lt;i&gt;S&lt;/i&gt;-methyl-5'-thioadenosine&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="/compound?orgid=META&amp;id=CH33ADO"&gt;5'-deoxyadenosine&lt;/a&gt; [&lt;a href="http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/31950558"&gt;North20&lt;/a&gt;].</comment>
